A||N||9||KissMySSFiero||How difficult is it to remove the front susp. cradle on an 88??||||1||
Z||000000||KissMySSFiero||07-11-2001||08:09 PM||||How difficult is it to remove the front susp. cradle on an 88??<P>how long would this take?<BR>who has done this?<BR>Tia<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||07-11-2001||08:33 PM||||It's very easy. There are eight total bolts holding the cradle to the frame. Two in the front near the sway bar, four behind the spring perch, and two near the back towards the end of the frame. You have to drain the coolant system and remove the metal coolant pipes and some brake line connectors hidden near the top of the cradle. I removed the universal joint on the steering column and pull the cradle down a little so I could reach the universal near the rack and pinion unit. It was easiest that way for me. You will need a jack to help you slowly lower the cradle so you can watch out for those brake lines. That’s pretty much it. <P>Than you can sand everything down and replace all the bushings and hardware with ease. That is what I did.<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Will||07-11-2001||10:07 PM||||Pull the plastic bucket that makes up the floor of the front compartment first. Doing this lets you get to the top of thye crossmember and the steering shaft. It makes the job <I>much</I> easier.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||07-11-2001||11:00 PM||||Yep... Just like they said. I agree with pulling the spare tire tub. It takes a few minutes, but makes life a <B>lot</B> easier underneath.<P>To undo the steering shaft; from inside the car there are three small screws holding a rubber sleeve where the shaft goes thru the floor board. Take them out so the rubber sleeve can slide up into the passenger compartment. Disconnect the lower u-joint where it goes into the rack.<P>Didn't really time it when I did it. 2 or 3 beers to get it out. Hardest part was the rusty bolts.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||07-11-2001||11:02 PM||||Hey 88formula, 2 + 4 + 2 = <B>8</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Otherwise, a great description.<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000005||Standard||07-12-2001||01:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>2 or 3 beers to get it out. Hardest part was the rusty bolts.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> lol!  I think that's the standard measurment of repair time, isn't it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">        <BR>1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed<P><FONT SIZE="1">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto<BR><FONT COLOR="red">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||KissMySSFiero||07-12-2001||03:54 PM||||i didnt think it would be too difficult.  thanks for the tip on the spare tire. my main concern is i bent the flange thingy(no really thats what the helm manual calls it) that holds the lower control car to the cradle.  anyone have experience with that.  its off by about a half inch or so.   id have to look again.  but its far enough out that i my caster cant be adjusted to spec.  it hasnt caused any problems as far as tire wear so its been like that a while.  i want to get it fixed and alligned this week because im leaving to go to fla next week.  only problem is i on ly have one day to do it for the most part(too busy lately)  i dotn want to start this if its going to be a 3 day job.   well see how it goes.  im gonna be takin pics this weekend too.  =Þ  <BR>thanks for the tips.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||14
Z||000007||DRH||07-12-2001||04:31 PM||||I'm not sure I follow you on the "flange thingy".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> How did you bend them? How is this effecting caster? Are you saying the whole lower control arm is knocked towards the rear (or front) of the car?<P>Redoing the whole front end is not a day job. Unless you work faster than I do <B>and</B> have a lot better luck with getting stuff loose that's been rusting in place for 13 years or so.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000008||KissMySSFiero||07-12-2001||06:23 PM||||if you can see it, the first pic is the damaged side.  its bent to the rear of the car. the second pic is the drivers side and its fine.  i don think it will take much to bend it back.  but it looks like ill wait till i can afford to have the car down for a while.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-066s.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-063s.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000009||DRH||07-12-2001||06:47 PM||||Ouch!<P>Those flanges bend fairly easily. I bent one of mine some while trying to beat the bolt loose. It went right back with a few good hits from a hammer. The biggest problem will be figuring out when it's where it belongs. Anybody else know how close to "perfect" it needs to be to eliminate any ill effects?<P>If I were you, I would consider getting another lower control arm. Chances are it is bent some also.<P>If the alignment is way off you might want to try to staighten it out the best you can before your trip. It sure doesn't sound like you'll have time to tackle the whole thing though...<P><BR>||||reg||1
